[#:seon.task{:name "an-unreadable-odd-map-is-not-one-form"
             :plan "`seon.edit/single-form?` throws instead of answering false when its source holds a map literal with an odd number of forms: `(seon.edit/single-form? \"{:a 1 :b}\")` throws IllegalArgumentException \"No value supplied for key: :b\" against its own `:boolean` output, and so do \"{:a}\", \"[{:a}]\" and \"(f {:a 1 :b})\" (observed in the JVM on default 6299bcda4). `seon.edit/parse-root` parses the odd map without complaint, `rewrite-clj.zip/sexpr-able?` is true for it, and `rewrite-clj.zip/sexpr` inside `seon.edit/location-sexpr` throws, so `seon.edit/valid-form-operation?` also throws on a form-edit request whose replacement holds one. Source holding an odd map anywhere is not readable, and `seon.sci.reader/read`, the one reader, already says so: it answers one read event carrying `:seon.sci.reader/error` for \"{:a 1 :b}\" and \"[{:a}]\", and events with no error for readable source such as \"(a)\", \"::x\", \"#?(:clj 1)\" and \"#(inc %)\". `seon.edit/single-form` decides readability with that reader, and an unreadable source gets the refusal it already gives a source with the wrong form count, so `seon.edit/single-form?` answers false; every readable source answers exactly what it answers today (\"#_x (a)\" stays false: its form count is a separate question, out of scope). The property generates odd-count maps with `clojure.test.check.generators/vector` of `clojure.test.check.generators/keyword` under `clojure.test.check.generators/such-that` `clojure.core/odd?` of `clojure.core/count`, and checks them with `clojure.test.check/quick-check` under `seon.test-support/assert-check!`. Read `seon.edit/single-form`, `seon.edit/single-form?`, `seon.edit/location-sexpr`, `seon.edit/parse-root` and `seon.sci.reader/read`."
             :children #{[:seon.task/sym seon.edit/prove-an-unreadable-odd-map-is-not-one-form]
                         [:seon.task/sym seon.edit/implement-an-unreadable-odd-map-is-not-one-form]}}
 #:seon.task{:name "prove-an-unreadable-odd-map-is-not-one-form"
             :step :prove
             :product #{seon.edit-test/an-odd-map-anywhere-is-not-one-form
                        seon.edit-test/every-source-holding-an-odd-map-is-not-one-form}
             :instructions "In `seon.edit-test`, add two deftests, the step's declared product, each calling the public `seon.edit/single-form?`. (1) A table named an-odd-map-anywhere-is-not-one-form, `[source expected]` cases asserted with `clojure.core/=` on `(seon.edit/single-form? source)`: [\"(a)\" true], [\"x\" true], [\"(a) ;; c\" true], [\"{:a 1}\" true], [\"#?(:clj 1)\" true], [\"#(inc %)\" true], [\"::x\" true], [\"(a) (b)\" false], [\"\" false], and the red cases [\"{:a 1 :b}\" false], [\"{:a}\" false], [\"[{:a}]\" false], [\"(f {:a 1 :b})\" false] (each throws today). Its assertion message is short fixed prose, never a printed value. (2) A property named every-source-holding-an-odd-map-is-not-one-form, with `clojure.test.check/quick-check` 300 and a fixed `:seed` (use 20261013) under `seon.test-support/assert-check!`: for every source built from ks, an odd-count vector of 1 to 7 keywords from `(clojure.test.check.generators/such-that (comp odd? count) (clojure.test.check.generators/vector clojure.test.check.generators/keyword 1 7))`, and a wrapping w from `(clojure.test.check.generators/choose 0 2)`, where the map text is `(str \"{\" (clojure.string/join \" \" ks) \"}\")` and w 0 leaves it bare, 1 wraps it as `[` map `]` and 2 as `(f ` map `)`, `(false? (seon.edit/single-form? source))`. Tag both `^{:seon/tasks #{'seon.edit/implement-an-unreadable-odd-map-is-not-one-form}}`. Run them red on your branch: the four odd-map rows and the property (seed 20261013 fails at its first test, shrinking to \"{:A :A :A}\") are red; the other rows are green."}
 #:seon.task{:name "implement-an-unreadable-odd-map-is-not-one-form"
             :step :implement
             :needs #{[:seon.task/sym seon.edit/prove-an-unreadable-odd-map-is-not-one-form]}
             :instructions "Make the table and the property green by changing `seon.edit/single-form` only, plus `[seon.sci.reader :as reader]` in the `seon.edit` ns requires (`seon.sci.reader` requires neither `seon.edit` nor anything that does). After `seon.edit/parse-root` succeeds and before any location is turned into a form, read the source once with `(seon.sci.reader/read {:seon.sci.reader/text source :seon.config.eval.result/max-source (count source)})` (the whole text is already held, as `seon.render.value` and `seon.turn` read it); when it answers a `:seon.sci.reader/failure` (not a vector) or any event carrying `:seon.sci.reader/error`, return the same `seon.error.refusal/diagnostic` refusal the wrong form count returns. No try or catch. Keep `seon.edit/single-form`'s contract and `seon.edit/single-form?` as they are, so every readable source answers what it answers today, and `seon.edit-test/form-edit-preserves-every-unselected-byte`, `seon.edit-test/form-edit-records-its-span-in-utf8-bytes`, `seon.edit-test/form-failures-never-fall-back-to-text`, `seon.edit-test/selectors-refuse-ambiguity-and-use-parsed-dispatch` and `my.edit-test/form-operation-relation-is-structural-and-open` stay green."}]
